# Harness project

This repo is a file agent: an OpenAI-compatible chat loop, tools confined to one workspace, and a JSONL trace in that workspace's `session.log`.

- `src/harnh3x/config.py` holds `PROVIDER`, `API_KEY`, `API_URL`, `MAX_TOKENS`, `CONTEXT_LIMIT`, `MODEL`, `MAX_TURNS`, `COMPACT_AT`, `MAX_TOOL_RESULT`, the fetch/search/feed limits, `SHELL_TIMEOUT` and `SHELL_MAX_TIMEOUT`, the file listing and search caps, `PDF_MAX_PAGES`, `PREVIEW_ROWS`, `MEMORY_FILE`, `PLAN_FILE`, `TRANSCRIPT_FILE`, `WIKIPEDIA_LANG`, and `BASE_DIR` (default `~/.harnh3x`, expanded when it is absolute or starts with `~`). Sessions live in `BASE_DIR/workspaces`. `MEMORY_FILE` is `BASE_DIR/memory.md`, shared across sessions. `~/.config/harnh3x/harnh3x.conf` (or `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/harnh3x/harnh3x.conf`) can set the API key, API URL, and those tunables except `MEMORY_FILE`, `PLAN_FILE`, and `TRANSCRIPT_FILE`. A non-empty process environment variable overrides the file, and a working-directory `.env` fills variables that are not already set. `HARNH3X_CONFIG` selects another file; an empty value skips it. `provider` is `openai` (default) or `anthropic`. Startup exits when `api_key` is unset, and when `api_url` is unset for `openai`. For `anthropic`, the key is `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` when that variable is set, otherwise `api_key`; `OPENAI_API_KEY` does not override it. `api_url` defaults to `https://api.anthropic.com`. `max_tokens` defaults to 8192. `context_limit` is optional; Claude compaction uses 200000 when it is unset. `--yolo` stays a launch flag.
- `src/harnh3x/anthropic_api.py` translates the stored transcript to the Anthropic Messages API and maps the stream back into the same assistant message. `get_client()` returns that client when `provider` is `anthropic`.
- `src/harnh3x/prompt.py` builds the system prompt: date and OS, a one-line workspace listing, the saved memory keys, the prompt contract, and the skill menu. It accepts `now` for tests and `yolo` to add the unsandboxed-session sentence.
- `src/harnh3x/tools.py` defines the tool schema and the sandbox. `TOOLS` is the full domain catalog.
- `src/harnh3x/skills/` holds `SkillRegistry` plus one `SKILL.md` per skill: `file_ops`, `shell`, `python`, `coding`, `research`, `reference`, `api`, `documents`, `data`, `memory`, and `tasks`. Every tool belongs to exactly one skill. The loop sends `load_skill`, `unload_skill`, and schemas for loaded skills only; several skills can be loaded at once.
- `src/harnh3x/agent.py` owns `Session` and `run`. `Session.reset()` starts a new conversation in a new workspace, keeping the model and `yolo`. `Session.resume()` reloads a workspace's `transcript.json`, replays skill loads, and refreshes the system prompt. `yolo` stays a launch flag and is not stored in the transcript.
- `src/harnh3x/cli.py` is the CLI, exposed as the `harnh3x` console script. `--yolo` disables the seatbelt sandbox: read tools may open any path, and shell and Python may run any program, including sudo. File mutation tools stay in the workspace. A tty session uses Textual (`src/harnh3x/tui.py`): a header whose title is Harnh3x followed by the package version, then the workspace, model, and context used against the model's limit, then the transcript. In yolo mode the header’s first line is `YOLO — sandbox off` in bright yellow, and that mark stays after Ctrl+N and `/resume`. Plain stdout prints the same warning before the workspace and model. `--answer-only` stays the final answer only. The composer takes Enter to submit and Shift+Enter for a newline. Ctrl+Q and `/exit` quit. Ctrl+N starts a new session in a new workspace and refreshes the header path. Ctrl+H hides or shows every thinking box, tool box, and compaction note, including ones added while they are hidden. `/help` opens a box of commands and hotkeys that Escape closes. `/resume` opens a list of past sessions and restores that transcript. `/compact` forces a context compaction. Each model round's tool calls share a bordered box, in the order the API produced them. Thinking and the answer update while the completion streams; each thinking box keeps the last three lines until a click expands it, and Ctrl+T expands the latest one. A context compaction shows Compacting context… while the summary runs, then a Context compacted note, and the agent answer is rendered as Markdown. One-shot on a tty starts that view before the request so tokens are visible as they arrive, and waits for Enter to close when the turn included reasoning. Plain stdout writes reasoning and the answer as the tokens arrive. `/resume` reprints a finished transcript in that same order, with the collapsed thinking panel for a finished reasoning block. Piped input and `--answer-only` stay plain stdout. `--model` with no name uses the Textual list on a tty and a numbered prompt otherwise. Tests live in `tests/test_harnh3x.py`.
- Export new public symbols from `src/harnh3x/__init__.py` `__all__`.

Poetry with `package-mode = true` and a `poetry-core` build backend so pip and pipx install the `harnh3x` script. Pytest uses `pythonpath = ["src"]`. Format with Black. Do not commit `src/.env`.

A new tool, or a looser path or shell check, needs a matching test.

```python
# BAD: a second model constant next to the loop
MODEL = "other"

# GOOD: change the constant in src/harnh3x/config.py
from harnh3x.config import MODEL
```
